{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"ab19cb14912f397c7bfe78c4ff87aa9f0c2d5231105aafe90d2cd21e7acfd0f0","digest":{"component_or_area":"store lock acquisition","key_entities":["lock.py:acquire()","lock.py:write_lock()","event_append.py:write_lock()","txn.py:_acquire_write_lock","push.py:write_lock()","REBAR_LOCK_RETRIES","_write_path_retries()","LockTimeout"],"problem_keywords":["write loss","lock timeout","terminal budget","contention","retry"],"propositions":["A store write whose lock acquire times out is permanently discarded with no retry or queue, losing the write durably.","The current acquire() budget is terminal: one deadline shared by both fcntl and mkdir legs, with no re-attempt mechanism after timeout.","Holder duration (not writer count) drives write loss; a single holder exceeding the 60s budget causes all waiting writers to fail regardless of fairness.","Bounded retry-with-backoff inside acquire() converts write loss into latency, re-attempting only the lock acquisition without replaying the write body.","Five call sites opt into retries via REBAR_LOCK_RETRIES (default 2, clamped [0,10]); all others keep fail-fast via retries=0 default."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787888000271734001,"uuid":"e26e6779-ae9b-4598-92f8-db6181b63244"}